Ephesians 6:12 is a verse from the New Testament of the Bible, and it reads:

&quot;For we do not wrestle against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the cosmic powers over this present darkness, against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenly places.&quot;

This verse emphasizes the spiritual nature of the struggles and challenges Christians face. It highlights that their true battles are not against human beings but against spiritual entities and forces that oppose God&#x27;s will. The verse is often interpreted as a call to recognize the deeper, unseen spiritual realities behind the difficulties in life and to approach these struggles with spiritual tools, such as prayer and faith.

